  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=1\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=4\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=1\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=1.5\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{3}=3\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin.",
  "worked_solution": "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},\u2026,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1, & \\,{m}_{3} & =4, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =1.5, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1.5+4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =5+1.5+12 \\\\  & =18.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $18.5\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$",
